# Citation metadata for the SIMPLER Descriptive App.
# GitHub shows a "Cite this repository" button from this file, and Zenodo reads it
# (authors, title, licence) when it archives a release.
# TODO: add ORCID iDs if available
#       (e.g.   orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000").

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SIMPLER data, please cite the SIMPLER white paper
  (doi:10.1007/s10654-026-01455-6) and follow the SIMPLER publication policy.
  If you reuse or adapt this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
title: "SIMPLER Descriptive App"
abstract: >-
  An R Shiny application for researchers preparing a data application to SIMPLER
  (Swedish Infrastructure for Medical Population-Based Life-Course and Environmental
  Research). It lets users browse the available variables, estimate how many participants
  match a combination of variables using an anonymised dataset, estimate the cost of a
  request, and download the selected variables.
